Z||000001||isthiswhereiputausername?||10-01-2001||08:38 PM||||Almost any FWD tranny will.. I have one out of a 85 skylark in mine  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fformula88||10-01-2001||09:37 PM||||Most of the FWD trannies are the same... just be sure the bolt holes in the bell housing will match up to your engine.  Also be sure you get one that will talk well with your computer (i.e. a 4 spd od might not be a good idea).  The one you want is the Hydramatic 125c I believe (anybody confirm or correct me?)||||reg||1
Z||000003||yo_sweet||10-01-2001||10:43 PM||||thnaks guys do i need to drop the cradle otu to remove the tranny? is there another way?||||reg||1
Z||000004||MinnGreenGT||10-01-2001||11:31 PM||||Dropping the cradle isn't necessary, but certainly is worth it when it comes to working on it.  The 125 is the stock Fiero 3 Spd Auto.  You CAN get a 440t4 to work with the Fiero farily easily (need some creativity as well).  You'll just need to rewire the TCC to get it to operate correctly (something I still haven't done yet).<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg">         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fullstaff.gif">     <BR>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
